-- WARNING: COPY ------------- errors/copy_shared_5.march

`List.map` builds a new copy instead of reusing `xs` in place, because a closure captured `xs`. [copy_shared]
A closure keeps its own reference to every value it captures, since it may run more than once, so a call inside it never holds the only reference to `xs`.

9 |     fn () -> List.map(xs, fn x -> x + 1)
                          ^^


    this closure captures `xs`:

9 |     fn () -> List.map(xs, fn x -> x + 1)
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    run `march --explain copy_shared`


